 0030   0006    '----- GAME6.BAS: VGA scene module (uGL 0.23b, src\ugl). Sixth 
                code module ->
 0030   0006    '----- its own 64K code segment. Pure library (no COMMON SHARED
                ): the ONLY module
 0030   0006    '----- that includes UGL.BI and talks to the library; the rest 
                of the game stays
 0030   0006    '----- in CGA land and just CALLs the scenes.
 0030   0006    '-----
 0030   0006    '----- VgaOpen: uglInit ONCE per run (the 0.23b release lib ref
                uses every VESA
 0030   0006    '-----   mode from the third uglInit/uglEnd cycle on - UGLTEST6
                /7/8) + the video
 0030   0006    '-----   mode ladder -- VESA 640x480x256 two pages -> one page 
                -> plain VGA
 0030   0006    '-----   320x200x256 (needs neither VESA nor EMS). Returns the 
                video DC handle
 0030   0006    '-----   (0 = nothing available, skip the scene) and reports th
                e mode reached in
 0030   0006    '-----   xr/yr/np. Remembers the BIOS mode it was called from. 
                Whenever the
 0030   0006    '-----   two-page VESA rung is NOT reached it appends a report 
                to VGA.LOG (VgaDiag:
 0030   0006    '-----   free memory, EMS, the raw VESA answers - 4F00h info bl
                ock, 4F01h mode
 0030   0006    '-----   101h, and if no 640x480 rung worked a manual 4F02h/4F0
                6h/4F07h probe) so
 0030   0006    '-----   a real 486 can tell us why. DOSBox-X's S3 never writes
                 it.
 0030   0006    '----- VgaClose: uglRestore (which only knows the mode uGL was 
                INITIALISED in, the
 0030   0006    '-----   text mode at the logo) then INT 10h sets the caller's 
                mode back. The CGA
 0030   0006    '-----   framebuffer does NOT survive a switch: an in-game call
                er must redraw the
 0030   0006    '-----   room afterwards (GAME.BAS domanual -> invret does). ug
                lEnd is left to
 0030   0006    '-----   uGL's own exit hook.
 0030   0006    '----- VgaPalLoad / VgaPalApply / VgaPalBMP / VgaPalBlack: the 
                hardware palette
 0030   0006    '-----   from an 8-bit BMP's own colour table (54-byte header +
                 256 BGRA entries),
 0030   0006    '-----   kept in mPal() so it can be applied scaled (fades) / a
                ll black. BMPs are
 0030   0006    '-----   drawn with BMPOPT.NO332 so their indices are kept as a
                uthored.
 0030   0006    '----- VgaHold: TIMER wait (midnight-safe) that any key cuts sh
                ort.
 0030   0006    '----- VgaSync: wait for the NEXT vertical retrace (leave the c
                urrent one first;
 0030   0006    '-----   a bare WAIT &H3DA, 8 returns at once when already insi
                de a retrace).
 0030   0006    '----- LogoShow: tenthplay logo before the intro, darkv-bas sty
                le: cut in, hold
 0030   0006    '-----   2 s, any key ends it, cut to black. TPLOGO.BMP (640x48
                                                                      PAGE   2
                                                                      15 Sep 26
                                                                      18:43:57
Offset  Data    Source Line      Microsoft (R) QuickBASIC Compiler Version 4.50

                0) on the VESA
 0030   0006    '-----   rungs, TPLOG320.BMP (320x200) on the mode-13h rung.
 0030   0006    '-----
 0030   0006    '----- ManualShow (Tab in the game): the VGA manual. It opens 8
                00x600x256 (one
 0030   0006    '-----   page = 600 KB, fits a 1 MB card) and flips through the
                 composed views
 0030   0006    '-----   MANP00.BMP, MANP01.BMP, ... - each a complete 800x600 
                image made from the
 0030   0006    '-----   instruction-manual PDF (tools\compose_all.py): MANP00 
                = front cover
 0030   0006    '-----   centred, the inside pages shown with the NEXT page cut
                 off at the right edge
 0030   0006    '-----   and a soft binding crease at the seam (Tunic-style), t
                he last MANP = back
 0030   0006    '-----   cover centred. A view is drawn whole at (0,0); there i
                s no scrolling and no
 0030   0006    '-----   second page (the Cirrus VESA BIOS honours neither), so
                 a page turn just
 0030   0006    '-----   fades through black to the next view. Keys: Left/Up/Pg
                Up = previous,
 0030   0006    '-----   Right/Down/PgDn = next, Home/End, Tab/Esc = close. Mou
                se (game mouse=1):
 0030   0006    '-----   click the left half of the screen = previous, right ha
                lf = next. If 800x600
 0030   0006    '-----   is unavailable it falls back to ManualSimple (the old 
                MANnnH/L pages).
 0030   0006    DEFINT A-Z
 0030   0006    '$INCLUDE: 'UGL.BI'
 0030   0006    ''
 0030   0006    '' ugl.bi -- UGL routines
 0030   0006    ''
 0030   0006    
 0030   0006    Const UGL.TRUE%     = -1%
 0030   0006    Const UGL.FALSE%    = 0%
 0030   0006    
 0030   0006    Const DCTSIZE%      = 64%
 0030   0006    '' dc types:
 0030   0006    Const UGL.MEM%      = 0% * DCTSIZE%
 0030   0006    Const UGL.BNK%      = 1% * DCTSIZE%
 0030   0006    Const UGL.EMS%      = 2% * DCTSIZE%
 0030   0006    
 0030   0006    Const FMTSIZE%      = 128%
 0030   0006    '' color formats:
 0030   0006    Const UGL.8BIT%     = 0% * FMTSIZE%
 0030   0006    Const UGL.15BIT%    = 1% * FMTSIZE%
 0030   0006    Const UGL.16BIT%    = 2% * FMTSIZE%
 0030   0006    Const UGL.32BIT%    = 3% * FMTSIZE%
 0030   0006    
 0030   0006    '' buffer formats for uglRow Read/Write/SetPal routines
 0030   0006    Const UGL.BF.8BIT%  = 0% * 2%
 0030   0006    Const UGL.BF.15BIT% = 1% * 2%
 0030   0006    Const UGL.BF.16BIT% = 2% * 2%
 0030   0006    Const UGL.BF.32BIT% = 3% * 2%
